<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑστέρα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑστέρη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>womb,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aph.</u>
				5.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.13.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.2
			</span></i>, etc.; freq. in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑστέραι,</span>
			
				Ion.
			 gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				515
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				91c
			</span></i>:—with a play on the Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑστέρα</span> (the second woman), <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				13.585d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>ovary</i> of animals, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				720a26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HA</u>
				511a22
			</span></i>; of birds, ib.<i><span class="en">
				564b21
			</span></i>; reptiles, ib.<i><span class="en">
				508a13
			</span></i>; fishes, ib.<i><span class="en">
				566a7
			</span></i>. (Lit. <i>the upper</i> or <i>protruding</i> part, Skt.
				<i>úttaras</i> 'upper', 
				Comp. of
			
			<i>úd</i> 'upwards'; so also Skt.
			<i>udáram</i> 'belly'; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕστρος: γαστήρ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; or perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὑ.</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτρα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δελφύς</span>) <i>the back part.</i>)</div>
